nir/algebraic: fold constant sin/cos exactly with lower_sincos

The lower_sincos polynomial also replaced fsin/fcos of constants before
constant folding saw them; tan(1.57) = sin/cos then missed the exact
value by far more than GLSL precision (piglit glsl-fs-tan-2).  Lower only
non-constant arguments.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

diff -urNp a/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_algebraic.py b/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_algebraic.py
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_algebraic.py	2026-10-11 20:23:18.579293924 +0200
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_algebraic.py	2026-10-11 20:23:18.580293936 +0200
@@ -1908,8 +1908,9 @@ optimizations.extend([
    (('fsqrt', a), ('frcp', ('frsq', a)), 'options->lower_fsqrt'),
    (('frcp(contract)', ('frsq', a)), ('fsqrt', a), '!options->lower_fsqrt'),
    # Trig
-   (('fsin', a), lowered_sincos(0.5), 'options->lower_sincos'),
-   (('fcos', a), lowered_sincos(0.75), 'options->lower_sincos'),
+   # Constant arguments are folded exactly instead of approximated.
+   (('fsin', 'a(is_not_const)'), lowered_sincos(0.5), 'options->lower_sincos'),
+   (('fcos', 'a(is_not_const)'), lowered_sincos(0.75), 'options->lower_sincos'),
    # Boolean simplifications
    (('ieq', a, True), a),
    (('ine(is_not_used_by_if)', a, True), ('inot', a)),
